For the self-adjoint Hamiltonians <a href="#eq:main-H" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:main-H">[eq:main-H]</a>, the normalized ground states of the even periodic rings have a subsequence, as $L\to\infty$, converging on every local operator to a state $\omega$. Every such limit satisfies $$\label{eq:local-limit-gap}
 \omega(A^*[H,A])\ge\frac{\log20}{784}
 \bigl(\omega(A^*A)-|\omega(A)|^2\bigr)$$ for every local operator $A$.
